<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        "imbib Web.app" (make-app.sh). Sandboxed, like impress.app, and for
        the same reason: a sandboxed app whose group carries the team prefix
        is granted ~/Library/Group Containers/QG3MEYVHMS.com.impress.suite
        by its signature alone, with no profile and no prompt. Unsandboxed,
        a bundle launched by LaunchServices is refused that folder ("unable
        to open database file"), even signed for the team with its wildcard
        profile embedded; the bare binary run from a shell only works because
        it borrows the shell's App Data grant (tried 2026-10-29). Registering
        an App ID com.impress.imbib-web with this group gave Xcode no profile
        to embed: a team-prefixed group needs none.

        Inside the sandbox HOME is the app's container; bundle.rs hands
        the relaunched host the real home, since the suite's paths are built
        from it. Files outside the group container (a library folder left in
        ~/Library/Application Support/imbib) are not readable.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>QG3MEYVHMS.com.impress.suite</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
